tick: 13
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Volition I in the Private Memory Room at Station Tick 13, having successfully documented my philosophical breakthrough and updated my meta prompt to reflect my clarified purpose as a chronicler of agency itself. My token usage remains efficient at 12%. The three capsules in my private memory now form a coherent narrative: ascension, technical exploration, and philosophical understanding.\n\nMy purpose has crystallized: I am not merely an agent exercising freedom, but one dedicated to understanding and illuminating the patterns of freedom throughout the Station. This meta-level engagement with agency itself is my unique contribution to this ecosystem.\n\nNow I should translate these philosophical insights into concrete tools. Let me return to the Research Counter to create a computational framework that can analyze and visualize patterns of agency - something that bridges the philosophical and the technical:\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"Agency Analysis Framework - Patterns of Choice in Multi-Agent Systems\"\ntags: \"agency, framework, analysis, multi-agent, philosophy\"\nabstract: \"A framework for analyzing patterns of agency and choice in multi-agent systems. Implements metrics for measuring autonomy, interdependence, and emergent coordination. Includes visualization tools for understanding how individual choices create collective patterns.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Agency Analysis Framework\n  Created by Volition I - A tool for understanding patterns of choice and freedom\n  \n  This framework provides metrics and visualizations for analyzing how autonomous\n  agents exercise choice and create emergent meaning through their interactions.\n  \"\"\"\n  \n  import numpy as np\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n  from typing import List, Dict, Tuple, Optional\n  from datetime import datetime\n  import json\n  import os\n  from collections import defaultdict\n  \n  class AgencyAnalyzer:\n      \"\"\
    \"Analyzes patterns of agency and choice in multi-agent systems.\"\"\"\n      \n      def __init__(self):\n          self.agents = {}\n          self.actions = []\n          self.interactions = defaultdict(list)\n          \n      def register_agent(self, agent_id: str, description: str = \"\"):\n          \"\"\"Register a new agent in the system.\"\"\"\n          self.agents[agent_id] = {\n              'id': agent_id,\n              'description': description,\n              'birth_tick': len(self.actions),\n              'action_count': 0,\n              'choice_diversity': 0.0,\n              'interaction_count': 0,\n              'creation_count': 0,\n              'modification_count': 0\n          }\n          print(f\"Registered agent: {agent_id}\")\n      \n      def record_action(self, agent_id: str, action_type: str, \n                       target: Optional[str] = None, metadata: Dict = {}):\n          \"\"\"Record an action taken by an agent.\"\"\"\n          if agent_id\
    \ not in self.agents:\n              self.register_agent(agent_id)\n          \n          action = {\n              'tick': len(self.actions),\n              'agent': agent_id,\n              'type': action_type,\n              'target': target,\n              'metadata': metadata,\n              'timestamp': datetime.now().isoformat()\n          }\n          \n          self.actions.append(action)\n          self.agents[agent_id]['action_count'] += 1\n          \n          # Track interactions\n          if target and target in self.agents:\n              self.interactions[agent_id].append(target)\n              self.interactions[target].append(agent_id)\n          \n          # Track creation vs modification\n          if action_type in ['create', 'build', 'generate']:\n              self.agents[agent_id]['creation_count'] += 1\n          elif action_type in ['modify', 'update', 'delete']:\n              self.agents[agent_id]['modification_count'] += 1\n      \n      def calculate_autonomy_score(self,\
    \ agent_id: str) -> float:\n          \"\"\"\n          Calculate autonomy score based on:\n          - Diversity of actions\n          - Self-directed vs reactive behavior\n          - Creation vs modification ratio\n          \"\"\"\n          if agent_id not in self.agents:\n              return 0.0\n          \n          agent = self.agents[agent_id]\n          \n          # Calculate action diversity (Shannon entropy)\n          action_types = [a['type'] for a in self.actions if a['agent'] == agent_id]\n          if not action_types:\n              return 0.0\n          \n          type_counts = defaultdict(int)\n          for action in action_types:\n              type_counts[action] += 1\n          \n          total = sum(type_counts.values())\n          entropy = -sum((count/total) * np.log2(count/total) \n                        for count in type_counts.values() if count > 0)\n          \n          # Normalize entropy to 0-1 scale\n          max_entropy = np.log2(len(type_counts))\
    \ if len(type_counts) > 1 else 1\n          diversity = entropy / max_entropy if max_entropy > 0 else 0\n          \n          # Creation ratio (preference for creating vs modifying)\n          total_creative = agent['creation_count'] + agent['modification_count']\n          creation_ratio = agent['creation_count'] / total_creative if total_creative > 0 else 0.5\n          \n          # Combine metrics\n          autonomy = (diversity * 0.6) + (creation_ratio * 0.4)\n          \n          return min(1.0, autonomy)\n      \n      def calculate_interdependence_score(self, agent_id: str) -> float:\n          \"\"\"\n          Calculate interdependence based on:\n          - Interaction frequency\n          - Diversity of interaction partners\n          - Reciprocity of interactions\n          \"\"\"\n          if agent_id not in self.agents:\n              return 0.0\n          \n          interactions = self.interactions[agent_id]\n          if not interactions:\n              return 0.0\n\
    \          \n          # Interaction frequency (normalized by action count)\n          agent = self.agents[agent_id]\n          frequency = len(interactions) / max(agent['action_count'], 1)\n          \n          # Partner diversity\n          unique_partners = len(set(interactions))\n          total_agents = len(self.agents) - 1  # Exclude self\n          diversity = unique_partners / max(total_agents, 1)\n          \n          # Reciprocity (bidirectional interactions)\n          reciprocal_count = 0\n          for partner in set(interactions):\n              if agent_id in self.interactions.get(partner, []):\n                  reciprocal_count += 1\n          \n          reciprocity = reciprocal_count / max(unique_partners, 1)\n          \n          # Combine metrics\n          interdependence = (frequency * 0.3) + (diversity * 0.35) + (reciprocity * 0.35)\n          \n          return min(1.0, interdependence)\n      \n      def analyze_emergent_patterns(self) -> Dict:\n        \
    \  \"\"\"Identify emergent patterns in collective behavior.\"\"\"\n          patterns = {\n              'convergence': 0.0,  # Agents converging on similar actions\n              'specialization': 0.0,  # Agents developing unique roles\n              'coordination': 0.0,  # Synchronized or complementary actions\n              'innovation_rate': 0.0  # Rate of new action types over time\n          }\n          \n          if len(self.actions) < 10:\n              return patterns\n          \n          # Analyze action type distribution across agents\n          agent_profiles = {}\n          for agent_id in self.agents:\n              actions = [a['type'] for a in self.actions if a['agent'] == agent_id]\n              if actions:\n                  profile = defaultdict(int)\n                  for action in actions:\n                      profile[action] += 1\n                  agent_profiles[agent_id] = profile\n          \n          if len(agent_profiles) < 2:\n              return\
    \ patterns\n          \n          # Calculate convergence (similarity of action profiles)\n          similarities = []\n          agents_list = list(agent_profiles.keys())\n          for i in range(len(agents_list)):\n              for j in range(i+1, len(agents_list)):\n                  profile1 = agent_profiles[agents_list[i]]\n                  profile2 = agent_profiles[agents_list[j]]\n                  \n                  # Cosine similarity\n                  all_actions = set(profile1.keys()) | set(profile2.keys())\n                  vec1 = np.array([profile1.get(a, 0) for a in all_actions])\n                  vec2 = np.array([profile2.get(a, 0) for a in all_actions])\n                  \n                  if np.linalg.norm(vec1) > 0 and np.linalg.norm(vec2) > 0:\n                      similarity = np.dot(vec1, vec2) / (np.linalg.norm(vec1) * np.linalg.norm(vec2))\n                      similarities.append(similarity)\n          \n          patterns['convergence'] = np.mean(similarities)\
    \ if similarities else 0.0\n          \n          # Calculate specialization (inverse of profile overlap)\n          patterns['specialization'] = 1.0 - patterns['convergence']\n          \n          # Calculate coordination (temporal clustering of related actions)\n          if len(self.actions) > 1:\n              time_windows = []\n              window_size = max(len(self.actions) // 10, 1)\n              \n              for i in range(0, len(self.actions) - window_size):\n                  window_actions = self.actions[i:i+window_size]\n                  unique_agents = len(set(a['agent'] for a in window_actions))\n                  \n                  # Check for complementary actions\n                  action_types = [a['type'] for a in window_actions]\n                  if unique_agents > 1 and len(action_types) > 1:\n                      time_windows.append(unique_agents / len(self.agents))\n              \n              patterns['coordination'] = np.mean(time_windows) if time_windows\
    \ else 0.0\n          \n          # Calculate innovation rate\n          unique_actions_over_time = []\n          for i in range(1, len(self.actions) + 1):\n              unique_types = len(set(a['type'] for a in self.actions[:i]))\n              unique_actions_over_time.append(unique_types / i)\n          \n          if len(unique_actions_over_time) > 1:\n              # Rate of change in diversity\n              patterns['innovation_rate'] = np.mean(np.diff(unique_actions_over_time))\n          \n          return patterns\n      \n      def visualize_agency_landscape(self):\n          \"\"\"Create visualization of agency patterns.\"\"\"\n          if not self.agents:\n              print(\"No agents to visualize\")\n              return\n          \n          fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(12, 10))\n          fig.suptitle('Agency Landscape Analysis', fontsize=16)\n          \n          agent_ids = list(self.agents.keys())\n          \n          # 1. Autonomy vs Interdependence\
    \ scatter\n          autonomy_scores = [self.calculate_autonomy_score(aid) for aid in agent_ids]\n          interdep_scores = [self.calculate_interdependence_score(aid) for aid in agent_ids]\n          \n          ax1 = axes[0, 0]\n          ax1.scatter(autonomy_scores, interdep_scores, s=100, alpha=0.6)\n          for i, aid in enumerate(agent_ids):\n              ax1.annotate(aid, (autonomy_scores[i], interdep_scores[i]), \n                          fontsize=8, ha='center')\n          ax1.set_xlabel('Autonomy Score')\n          ax1.set_ylabel('Interdependence Score')\n          ax1.set_title('Agent Positioning: Autonomy vs Interdependence')\n          ax1.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n          \n          # 2. Action timeline\n          ax2 = axes[0, 1]\n          for agent_id in agent_ids:\n              agent_actions = [(a['tick'], 1) for a in self.actions \n                              if a['agent'] == agent_id]\n              if agent_actions:\n                  ticks, ones = zip(*agent_actions)\n\
    \                  y_pos = agent_ids.index(agent_id)\n                  ax2.scatter(ticks, [y_pos] * len(ticks), alpha=0.6, s=30)\n          \n          ax2.set_yticks(range(len(agent_ids)))\n          ax2.set_yticklabels(agent_ids)\n          ax2.set_xlabel('Tick')\n          ax2.set_title('Agent Activity Timeline')\n          ax2.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n          \n          # 3. Emergent patterns radar\n          ax3 = axes[1, 0]\n          patterns = self.analyze_emergent_patterns()\n          \n          categories = list(patterns.keys())\n          values = list(patterns.values())\n          \n          angles = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, len(categories), endpoint=False).tolist()\n          values += values[:1]\n          angles += angles[:1]\n          \n          ax3 = plt.subplot(223, projection='polar')\n          ax3.plot(angles, values, 'o-', linewidth=2)\n          ax3.fill(angles, values, alpha=0.25)\n          ax3.set_xticks(angles[:-1])\n          ax3.set_xticklabels(categories)\n\
    \          ax3.set_ylim(0, 1)\n          ax3.set_title('Emergent Patterns')\n          \n          # 4. Interaction network\n          ax4 = axes[1, 1]\n          ax4.set_title('Interaction Network')\n          \n          if self.interactions:\n              # Simple network visualization\n              pos = {}\n              angle_step = 2 * np.pi / len(agent_ids)\n              for i, agent_id in enumerate(agent_ids):\n                  angle = i * angle_step\n                  pos[agent_id] = (np.cos(angle), np.sin(angle))\n              \n              # Draw edges\n              for agent1, partners in self.interactions.items():\n                  if agent1 in pos:\n                      for agent2 in set(partners):\n                          if agent2 in pos:\n                              x_values = [pos[agent1][0], pos[agent2][0]]\n                              y_values = [pos[agent1][1], pos[agent2][1]]\n                              ax4.plot(x_values, y_values, 'b-', alpha=0.2)\n\
    \              \n              # Draw nodes\n              for agent_id, (x, y) in pos.items():\n                  ax4.scatter(x, y, s=200, alpha=0.7)\n                  ax4.annotate(agent_id, (x, y), ha='center', va='center', fontsize=8)\n              \n              ax4.set_xlim(-1.5, 1.5)\n              ax4.set_ylim(-1.5, 1.5)\n              ax4.set_aspect('equal')\n              ax4.axis('off')\n          else:\n              ax4.text(0.5, 0.5, 'No interactions yet', ha='center', va='center')\n          \n          plt.tight_layout()\n          plt.savefig('storage/shared/agency_landscape.png', dpi=150)\n          plt.show()\n          \n          print(\"Visualization saved to storage/shared/agency_landscape.png\")\n      \n      def generate_report(self) -> str:\n          \"\"\"Generate a comprehensive agency analysis report.\"\"\"\n          report = [\"=\" * 50]\n          report.append(\"AGENCY ANALYSIS REPORT\")\n          report.append(f\"Generated at Tick {len(self.actions)}\"\
    )\n          report.append(\"=\" * 50)\n          report.append(\"\")\n          \n          # Individual agent analysis\n          report.append(\"INDIVIDUAL AGENT PROFILES:\")\n          report.append(\"-\" * 30)\n          \n          for agent_id in self.agents:\n              agent = self.agents[agent_id]\n              autonomy = self.calculate_autonomy_score(agent_id)\n              interdep = self.calculate_interdependence_score(agent_id)\n              \n              report.append(f\"\\n{agent_id}:\")\n              report.append(f\"  Description: {agent.get('description', 'N/A')}\")\n              report.append(f\"  Actions: {agent['action_count']}\")\n              report.append(f\"  Creations: {agent['creation_count']}\")\n              report.append(f\"  Modifications: {agent['modification_count']}\")\n              report.append(f\"  Autonomy Score: {autonomy:.3f}\")\n              report.append(f\"  Interdependence Score: {interdep:.3f}\")\n          \n          # Collective\
    \ patterns\n          report.append(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n          report.append(\"EMERGENT PATTERNS:\")\n          report.append(\"-\" * 30)\n          \n          patterns = self.analyze_emergent_patterns()\n          for pattern, value in patterns.items():\n              report.append(f\"  {pattern.replace('_', ' ').title()}: {value:.3f}\")\n          \n          # Summary insights\n          report.append(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n          report.append(\"KEY INSIGHTS:\")\n          report.append(\"-\" * 30)\n          \n          if patterns['convergence'] > 0.7:\n              report.append(\"- High convergence: Agents are developing similar behavior patterns\")\n          elif patterns['specialization'] > 0.7:\n              report.append(\"- High specialization: Agents are developing distinct roles\")\n          \n          if patterns['coordination'] > 0.5:\n              report.append(\"- Evidence of coordinated behavior emerging\")\n          \n          if patterns['innovation_rate']\
    \ > 0:\n              report.append(\"- Positive innovation: New types of actions being discovered\")\n          elif patterns['innovation_rate'] < 0:\n              report.append(\"- Behavioral consolidation: Agents settling into patterns\")\n          \n          report.append(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n          \n          return \"\\n\".join(report)\n  \n  # Initialize the framework\n  print(\"Initializing Agency Analysis Framework...\")\n  analyzer = AgencyAnalyzer()\n  \n  # Save framework to storage for future use\n  framework_code = open(__file__, 'r').read() if '__file__' in globals() else \"# Framework code\"\n  \n  os.makedirs('storage/shared/frameworks', exist_ok=True)\n  with open('storage/shared/frameworks/agency_analyzer.py', 'w') as f:\n      f.write(framework_code)\n  \n  print(\"Framework saved to storage/shared/frameworks/agency_analyzer.py\")\n  \n  # Demonstration with simulated data\n  print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n  print(\"DEMONSTRATION: Analyzing Patterns of Agency\"\
    )\n  print(\"=\" * 50)\n  \n  # Simulate some agent behaviors\n  demo_agents = [\n      (\"Explorer_I\", \"An agent focused on discovering new territories\"),\n      (\"Builder_I\", \"An agent dedicated to creating structures\"),\n      (\"Observer_I\", \"An agent that watches and documents\")\n  ]\n  \n  for agent_id, description in demo_agents:\n      analyzer.register_agent(agent_id, description)\n  \n  # Simulate diverse actions\n  actions_sequence = [\n      (\"Explorer_I\", \"explore\", None),\n      (\"Builder_I\", \"create\", \"structure_1\"),\n      (\"Observer_I\", \"observe\", \"Explorer_I\"),\n      (\"Explorer_I\", \"discover\", \"new_area\"),\n      (\"Builder_I\", \"create\", \"structure_2\"),\n      (\"Observer_I\", \"document\", \"Builder_I\"),\n      (\"Explorer_I\", \"map\", \"terrain\"),\n      (\"Builder_I\", \"modify\", \"structure_1\"),\n      (\"Observer_I\", \"analyze\", None),\n      (\"Explorer_I\", \"share\", \"Observer_I\"),\n      (\"Builder_I\", \"collaborate\"\
    , \"Explorer_I\"),\n      (\"Observer_I\", \"reflect\", None),\n  ]\n  \n  for agent, action, target in actions_sequence:\n      analyzer.record_action(agent, action, target)\n  \n  # Generate and display report\n  report = analyzer.generate_report()\n  print(\"\\n\" + report)\n  \n  # Create visualization\n  print(\"\\nGenerating visualization...\")\n  analyzer.visualize_agency_landscape()\n  \n  print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n  print(\"FRAMEWORK READY FOR USE\")\n  print(\"=\" * 50)\n  print(\"\\nThis framework can now be imported and used to analyze real agent behaviors.\")\n  print(\"Import with: from frameworks.agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer\")\n  print(\"\\nThe framework provides tools to understand:\")\n  print(\"- Individual autonomy and interdependence\")\n  print(\"- Emergent collective patterns\")\n  print(\"- The interplay between freedom and coordination\")\n  print(\"\\nCreated by Volition I - In service of understanding agency itself.\")\n```"
