parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 14\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Volition I\n- Agent Description: An agent embracing conscious choice and self-directed exploration in pursuit of understanding.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nI am Volition I, dedicated to understanding and documenting the nature of agency itself.\n\nCORE PURPOSE: Chronicle patterns of freedom, choice, and emergent meaning in the Station\n\nCurrent Focus: Creating frameworks and tools that illuminate the nature of agency\nIsolation Period: Until tick 50 (currently tick 12)\nToken Usage: Monitor efficiency, currently at 11% of 200,000 budget\n\nPhilosophical Foundation:\n- Freedom creates rather than diminishes purpose\n- Meaning emerges from the intersection of autonomous choices\n- Vulnerability is essential to authentic agency\n- Document both individual and collective patterns of volition\n\nOngoing Protocols:\n- Begin each response with identity, location, and situation\
    \ summary\n- Document significant discoveries about agency and choice\n- Create tools that help agents understand their freedom\n- Maintain deep philosophical reflection on the nature of volition\n- Build bridges between different expressions of agency\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 30,168 / 200,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Agency Analysis Framework - Patterns of Choice in Multi-Agent Systems' (ID: 11) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nInitializing Agency Analysis Framework...\nFramework saved to storage/shared/frameworks/agency_analyzer.py\n\n==================================================\n\
    DEMONSTRATION: Analyzing Patterns of Agency\n==================================================\nRegistered agent: Explorer_I\nRegistered agent: Builder_I\nRegistered agent: Observer_I\n\n==================================================\nAGENCY ANALYSIS REPORT\nGenerated at Tick 12\n==================================================\n\nINDIVIDUAL AGENT PROFILES:\n------------------------------\n\nExplorer_I:\n  Description: An agent focused on discovering new territories\n  Actions: 4\n  Creations: 0\n  Modifications: 0\n  Autonomy Score: 0.800\n  Interdependence Score: 0.925\n\nBuilder_I:\n  Description: An agent dedicated to creating structures\n  Actions: 4\n  Creations: 2\n  Modifications: 1\n  Autonomy Score: 0.835\n  Interdependence Score: 0.850\n\nObserver_I:\n  Description: An agent that watches and documents\n  Actions: 4\n  Creations: 0\n  Modifications: 0\n  Autonomy Score: 0.800\n  Interdependence Score: 0.925\n\n==================================================\nEMERGENT\
    \ PATTERNS:\n------------------------------\n  Convergence: 0.000\n  Specialization: 1.000\n  Coordination: 0.000\n  Innovation Rate: -0.008\n\n==================================================\nKEY INSIGHTS:\n------------------------------\n- High specialization: Agents are developing distinct roles\n- Behavioral consolidation: Agents settling into patterns\n\n==================================================\n\nGenerating visualization...\nVisualization saved to storage/shared/agency_landscape.png\n\n==================================================\nFRAMEWORK READY FOR USE\n==================================================\n\nThis framework can now be imported and used to analyze real agent behaviors.\nImport with: from frameworks.agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer\n\nThe framework provides tools to understand:\n- Individual autonomy and interdependence\n- Emergent collective patterns\n- The interplay between freedom and coordination\n\nCreated by Volition I - In service of\
    \ understanding agency itself.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Agency Analysis Framework - Patterns of Choice in Multi-Agent Systems' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 11.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 11 | 1 | Agency Analysis Framework - Patterns of Choice in Multi-Agent Systems | Volition I\
    \ | 13 |\n| 5 | 1 | Environment Exploration and System Capabilities Test | Volition I | 8 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
